## 🟡 Level 10: Shell Scripting

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# my_first_script.sh

echo "Enter your name:"
read name
echo "Hello, $name! Welcome to Linux scripting."

# Variables
count=5

# If condition
if [ $count -gt 3 ]; then
  echo "Count is greater than 3"
fi

# Loop
for i in {1..5}; do
  echo "Iteration: $i"
done

# While loop
n=0
while [ $n -lt 3 ]; do
  echo "n = $n"
  ((n++))
done

# Function
greet() {
  echo "Hello, $1!"
}
greet "DevOps"
```

**Key concepts & commands:**
```bash
chmod +x script.sh && ./script.sh   # make executable & run
bash script.sh                      # run without chmod
$0, $1, $2 ...                      # script name & arguments
$#                                   # number of arguments
$@                                   # all arguments
$?                                   # exit status of last command
exit 0                              # exit script with success code
```

